So once upon a time, there was this girl who was the daughter of a Republican investment banker in the San Francisco Bay Area. She graduated from an all-girls high school in Palo Alto, Calif., and decided to pursue a college education at a girls school on the Upper East Side in Manhattan called Finch College. After attending classes there from 1957 to 1958, she transferred to the University of Miami, where she studied for a while before becoming a fashion model. She got married, then formed a band with her husband in San Francisco in 1965. It became one of the most popular psychedelic acts in the Bay Area. She joined up with another band in the fall of 1966, which quickly became one of the best-known and most popular rock bands in the country.
