Dennis Nahat will be revisiting ��The Nutcracker�� this December — sort of. ��The Terracotta Prince�� is a Chinese version of the fairy tale, and while the production Nahat has created with China��s Dalian Acrobatic Troupe still uses Tchaikovsky��s famous music, it promises to be a very different experience.
��There are acrobats, tumblers, kung fu artists and the snowflakes are on roller skates,�� said Nahat, Ballet San Jose��s former artistic director, who parted ways with the company in early 2012. ��There are no mice in this production.��
